==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|barley}}
From {{inh|en|enm|bere|id=barley|t=barley}}, from {{inh|en|ang|bere|t=barley}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*barī}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*baraz|t=barley}}. Compare {{cog|cy|bara||bread}}, {{cog|la|far||emmer}}, {{cog|sh|sc=Cyrl|бра̏шно}}/{{m|sh|brȁšno||flour}}, {{cog|sq|bar||grass}}, {{cog|grc|Φήρον||plant deity}}. ''See also'': {{m|en|barley}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/bɪə/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bere.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/bɪɚ/|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪə(ɹ)|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|beer|bier|bear|aa3=New Zealand,near-square}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|Scotland}} [[barley|Barley]], especially four-rowed barley or {{vern|six-rowed barley}}.

